# TTILocalityKnowledgeAnswer v1

A locality knowledge query is buyer-settlement-bound but Discord-identity-free and contributor-identity-free: no Discord user id, message id, message content, buyer email, precise home location, credential, secret, or token may appear anywhere in a buyer query's body, and no sensitive class may be flagged, or intake refuses outright rather than redacting. Matching discloses candidate contribution ids and license terms only — never the underlying knowledge and never contributor identity — until a human attribution reviewer approves discrete ppm weights, and every downstream stage re-verifies contribution rights fresh rather than trusting them forward from an earlier stage.

LocalityKnowledgeBuyerQuery(sourceProtocol=tti-direct-buyer-query-v1, buyerSettlement=urn:ame: enterprise identifier, question=bounded 20-500 chars, subject=bounded 3-120, geographicContext=bounded 2-120, temporalContext=optional bounded 2-120 or null, intendedUse in {local-practice-research, union-decision-support, institutional-memory}, noPersonalDataAttested=true, buyerTermsAcknowledged=true, requestedAt=parseable instant, budget={currency=USD, maximumMicros=non-negative safe integer}, no discordUserId/discordMessageId/messageContent/buyerEmail/preciseHomeLocation/credentials/secret/token key present anywhere in the body, sensitiveClasses=empty; matchingKey=NFKC-normalized lowercased whitespace-collapsed subject/geographicContext/temporalContext; personalDataIncluded=false, discordContentImported=false, legalEffect=buyer-demand-only-no-offer-sale-payment-entitlement-revenue-or-profit)
  -> LocalityKnowledgeMatchReceipt(query=same admitted query id, simulation=same query.simulation, eligible=active self-addressed TTIKnowledgeContribution records with license.resaleAllowed=true whose normalized subject and geographicContext equal query.matchingKey and whose normalized temporalContext equals query.matchingKey.temporalContext whenever the query names one, deduplicated by id and ordered by id — exact-equality matching only, never a relevance ranking or score; an empty eligible set refuses as no-active-resale-contribution-matches-bounded-context; candidateContributionIds=eligible ids, licenseProjection={contributionId, scope, resaleAllowed=true, attribution=pseudonymous-or-contributor-selected-public-attribution}, rightsCompatibleCount, humanAttributionReviewRequired=true, knowledgeDisclosedToBuyer=false, contributorIdentityDisclosed=false)
  -> KnowledgeAttributionReview(type=TTIKnowledgeAttributionReview, status=approved, humanReviewed=true, reviewerAuthority=urn:tti:office: pattern, reviewedAt=parseable instant, bound to same query.id/match.id and same simulation mode, weights name every match.candidateContributionIds exactly once with no duplicate or missing id, each weightPpm a positive safe integer paired with a bounded 20-500 rationale, weights sum to exactly 1,000,000 ppm)
  -> LocalityKnowledgeProductOffer(bound to same query/match/review ids, frozenContributionIds=match.candidateContributionIds=review's weighted contribution ids exactly — the same nonempty unique set both ways, each frozen contribution still self-addressed/active/resaleAllowed at freeze time, query.budget.currency=USD and maximumMicros>=10,000,000 (the fixed USD 10.00 price), validity window recordedAt<expiresAt<=recordedAt+P7D; price={currency=USD, unitAmountMicros=10,000,000, quantity=1, status=fixed-offer-not-payment}, frozenContributions={contributionId, licenseScope, attribution}, attributionWeights={contributionId, weightPpm}, deliveryPromise={artifact=one-source-traceable-locality-knowledge-answer, maximumWords=1500, correctionWindow=P30D, buyerLicense=internal-union-research-and-decision-support-no-resale-training-or-open-publication}, saleFormed=false, paymentObserved=false, entitlementCreated=false, revenueRecognized=false, profitRecognized=false).

The frozen offer is the exact boundary handed to the x402 settlement rail governed by its own contract (`content/contracts/locality-x402-sale.rml`, `lib/management/locality-x402-settlement.mjs`): that rail admits payment only against a self-addressed, unexpired offer still claiming no economic effect (saleFormed=false, paymentObserved=false, revenueRecognized=false) and whose simulation mode matches the payment configuration's, and it hands back exactly one thing this contract accepts as its own next input — a settled `TTIKnowledgeSaleReceipt` bound to that same offer id and buyer settlement, with paymentObserved=true, entitlementCreated=false, and revenueRecognized true only outside simulation.

  -> LocalityKnowledgeFulfillmentPackage(offer=same self-addressed frozen offer, sale=settled TTIKnowledgeSaleReceipt bound to the same offer.id and offer.buyerSettlement and to the same simulation mode, citedContributionIds=frozenContributionIds exactly — the same nonempty unique set both ways, every cited contribution re-checked self-addressed and resaleAllowed at fulfillment time (not trusted forward from the freeze), answer=bounded 80-10,000 characters and at most 1,500 words; provenance={contributionId, licenseScope, attribution, correctionStatus=active-at-preparation}, buyerLicense/correctionWindow carried from the offer's deliveryPromise, deliveryStatus=synthetic-nonposting under simulation else prepared-awaiting-authenticated-buyer-delivery, buyerDeliveryPosted=false, fulfillmentRecognized=false, revenueRecognized=false, profitRecognized=false).

Every stage closes before its successor. Malformed, unbound, mode-mismatched, or already-economically-claiming input settles as a typed TTILocalityKnowledgeProductRefusal{stage, reasons} at its seam, always carrying saleFormed=false, paymentObserved=false, revenueRecognized=false, profitRecognized=false. Rights are never trusted forward: match, review, freeze, and fulfillment are four independent resaleAllowed checks against contribution records read fresh each time, so a contribution revoked between stages closes the chain rather than being carried through on an earlier stage's finding. Contributor identity and the underlying knowledge itself stay undisclosed to the buyer at every stage before fulfillment (knowledgeDisclosedToBuyer=false, contributorIdentityDisclosed=false); a query naming any prohibited Discord, personal, or secret field, or any nonempty sensitiveClasses, is refused at intake rather than sanitized.
